cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "chatlens: text analysis of chat data from behavioural experiments"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Milella
    given-names: Nicola
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicomil/chatlens"
abstract: >-
  chatlens computes language measures, an LLM validation rubric and topic
  models over the conversations held during a behavioural experiment, and
  grafts them onto the choice datasets. An adapter turns one experiment's
  export into a canonical set of message tables; the analysis works from those
  tables alone, so the same pipeline runs on different studies.
keywords:
  - text analysis
  - experimental economics
  - content analysis
  - oTree
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0

